# No git index writes

The agent must **never** run commands that modify the git index, including:

- `git add` (any form: paths, `-A`, `-u`, `-p`, etc.)
- `git restore --staged`
- Any other command that stages or unstages files

`git reset` is fully banned separately (see `no-git-reset.mdc`) — never use it for unstaging or for any other purpose.

Leave all agent file edits **unstaged**. The user stages manually when ready.

This keeps **staged** (user baseline) separate from **unstaged** (new agent changes) for review.

If staging is needed before commit, list the file paths and tell the user what to run — do not run `git add` yourself.
